# Configuration

`internal/config` reads every setting. Precedence: defaults, then environment
variables, then flags. The server never loads a `.env` file: a host passes
variables in the `env` entry of its server config, and a shell exports them.

| Flag | Variable | Default | Validation |
|---|---|---|---|
| `--log-level` | `{{env_prefix}}_LOG_LEVEL` | `info` | `debug`, `info`, `warn` or `error` (any case) |
| `--version` | | off | Prints the version and exits |
| `--help` | | off | Prints usage and exits |

A blank variable counts as unset. An unknown flag or a positional argument
exits 2, and an invalid value exits 1, each with one line on stderr naming the
flag or setting.

## Logs

JSON on stderr, one record per line. At `info` the server logs `serving`, one
`request` record per tool call (method, tool, duration, whether it was a tool
error), any server fault with its cause, and `stopped` with the reason. At
`debug` it also logs list and discovery requests. The SDK's own records come
through at `warn` and above, tagged `"component":"mcp-sdk"`. Arguments and
results are never logged.

## Adding a setting

Add the flag and its `{{env_prefix}}_*` variable in `internal/config`, with a
default and validation, a precedence row in `TestLoadPrecedence`, a rejection
row in `TestLoadRejects`, a line in `.env.example` and a row in the table
above and in the README.
